From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: smit1237 <smit1237@gmail.com>
Date: Thu, 24 Sep 2026 08:05:04 +0300
Subject: [PATCH 24/30] time: rnsd starts without a synced clock; background
 NTP; optional DS3231 RTC

Reticulum must work with no internet at all (HaLow-, LAN- or WiFi-only
meshes), so rnsd no longer waits for a synced clock and starts at every
boot. lxmd and nomadnet stay opt-in (enabled=no); when enabled they no
longer wait for the clock either.

- S45ntpsync: non-blocking. Records the time source (/run/clock-source:
  rtc|ntp|browser) and runs a detached NTP one-shot (ntpdate -u -b,
  single-flight, step-locked against ntpd) that writes the RTC on
  success. New `resync` (hourly cron) re-verifies the clock with
  ntpdate -q and rewrites the RTC only from NTP-confirmed time.
- Optional DS3231 on the i2c5 bit-bang bus (GPIOA15 SCL / GPIOA27 SDA):
  kernel RTC_DRV_DS1307 + I2C_GPIO/ALGOBIT built in, rtc@68 in the DTS,
  and rtc-ds1307 keeps the oscillator-stop flag so an unset or brownout
  RTC is never used to set the clock.
- Portal: browser time seed also writes the RTC (even if never set);
  Time & Clock card shows source, RTC state and DS3231 temperature.
- Clock-step fallout handled: stale rnsd path tables, dnsmasq leases,
  LXMF messages/peers stored while the clock was unset (re-date patch).
- WAN tcp/4242 (rnsd TCPServerInterface) open by default with 22 and 80.
- python: psutil enabled; unicodedata made explicit (TLS/idna needs it).
